      "id": "e9",
      "name": "Table 8",
      "hidden": false,
      "parentId": null,
      "inheritedFrom": null,
      "kind": "table",
      "text": "Section\n\nStandard Outline\nProposed Technology Content\nWorkstream\n\n\nExecution Progress – Key Highlights\nKey achievements against All-Bank Technology Strategy and BNS Strategy (i.e., Marquee Programs)\nWS1\n\n\nF26 Financial Results\nTech Spend vs. Plan, with drivers of variance (standard Tech waterfall w/ commentary)\nWS3\n\n\nF26 KPI Results\nPerformance against F26 Board-Level KPIs and KRIs (standard Sept Board format)\n\n\n\nKey shifts impacting Strategy\nHeadwinds creating cost pressures (e.g., tokenomics, cost of compute – chips, AI race)\nWS2\n\n\nCompetitive Benchmarks\nHigh level benchmarks (e.g., spend level / profile, workforce, performance, complexity / legacy debt, “big bets”) and implications that point to F27+ strategic priorities\n\n\n\nStrategic Deep-Dives\n“Deep Dive” on Project Falcon, including objectives, path to F28 savings, overview of “big rocks” (build vs. buy, legacy infrastructure modernization, app rationalization, strategic workforce planning), and major modernization investments.\n\n\n\nMain F27+ strategic priorities \nEvolved Strategy Execution Placemat (highlighting key areas of focus for F27) and Marquee Programs\nWS 1\n\n\nFive-year outlook (financials, for Oct. only)\nF27 Financial Plan showing build of RTB and CTB spend, key drivers, and anticipated impact on spend level / mix (standard Tech waterfall w/ commentary)\nWS3\n\n\nKPIs (F26F and Proposed Changes) \nProposed changes to Board-level KPIs and KRIs (using standard Sept Board template)\nWS 1\n\n\nRisk Considerations\nTechnology-specific risks using non-financial risk categories (driven by 1B and GRM, using standard Sept Board template)\nOther",
